This package provides dump style mdz, which writes compressed,
crash-tolerant, appendable .mdz trajectories with the fields of dump custom.

It is not part of the LAMMPS distribution: the patch_lammps.sh script in the
lammps/ directory of the mdz repository puts it into a LAMMPS source tree.
Build LAMMPS with CMake and -D PKG_MDZ=ON. LAMMPS then builds the mdz library
from the mdz source tree that patched it (set MDZ_SOURCE_DIR to use another)
and links it in. The traditional make build is not supported.

Documentation, the file format and readers for Python, C and C++ and the
command line: https://github.com/peterspackman/mdz (lammps/README.md for the
dump style and its dump_modify keywords).

Author: Peter Spackman (peterspackman@fastmail.com)
